       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so toxicity would last a long time. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make this dose safe.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are the usual doses:\n- **2.5 mg daily** is a starting dose for frail patients or patients with hepatic impairment.\n- **5 mg daily** is the standard starting dose.\n- **10 mg daily** is the maximum.\n\nIf you meant one of these, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 50 mg, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me the clinical reason. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
